There are a few types of wands that I have always ready for use once I get
them; fire/lightning, sleep, teleportation, digging; those are primarily
defense or escape wands. Add wand(s) of death for the late game. Me being
a packrat, I carry all the junk with me, so I am no paragon. But building
stashes should fix that. A couple examples... Light very helpful throughout
the game (mines, dark rooms, Juiblex, or other open area). Magic missile
(which does no significant damage) to weaken a row of approaching monsters,
later e.g. to weaken the eels before finishing them in melee if necessary.
Striking similar to magic missile (but with more damage if it hits) and
in addition to retrieve loot from stoned monsters, or to clear a boulder
blocked path, or smash statues for books. Speed monster used just once to
become fast, later to restore your quickness in case of cockatrice or shade
incidents. Slow monster where you need it in iterated move/hit situations.
Undead turning useful if you rely on your pet. Cold mainly to bridge water,
but I save most charges for incidents on the Plane of Fire (to solidify the
lava). Cancellation to clean stacks of potions and scrolls, or prepare a
stack of projectiles for efficient enchantment. Create monster for sacfests.
Polymorph for polypile sessions (make invisible, magic missile, etc., are
amongst the poly-fodder), and in emergencies to get rid of a monster. How
many of the respective wands you should keep is your decision, depending
on your actual game. Stash the rest at appropriate places for poly-sessions
or where you can pick them up again for the next stage of your game where
those wands will be helpful.

